## Who they are

CyberAcme is a megacorporation in Marathon whose specialty is digital systems and artificial-intelligence features.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Every Marathon Runner shell ships with CyberAcme’s Onboard Navigation Intelligence (ONI) preinstalled to provide navigation assistance while the faction gathers information about the fate of the New Cascadia colony.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Bungie named CyberAcme among the factions available to play during the Server Slam preview event.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Press and the developer list CyberAcme as one of the six launch factions in Marathon.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}

## What they offer Runners

The CyberAcme armory supplies entry-level equipment such as ammunition, healing consumables, basic firearms, backpacks, and keys.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Reputation rewards from ranking up with CyberAcme include additional ammo, torso implants, and backpacks.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} In Update 1.0.0.4 (March 11, 2026) Bungie increased the starting ammunition quantities in free Sponsored Kits from several factions, including CyberAcme.{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Enhanced and Deluxe variants of CyberAcme Sponsored Kits become available at the Runner levels documented for Season 2.{{cite:kotaku-season-2}}

## Recent changes and activities

When the Cryo Archive zone is active, CyberAcme receives a pool that includes seven Cryo-specific contracts.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Bungie corrected a reward preview display bug affecting a CyberAcme contract in Update 1.1.0.1 (June 9, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}} Ahead of the Expedition Phase 1 update, CyberAcme joined other groups in a Runner non-aggression pact intended to address heightened UESC security on Tau Ceti IV.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

