## Who they are

Traxus OffWorld Industries is presented as an extremely powerful corporate entity within Marathon's setting.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Its operative Vulcan issues salvage-oriented tasks to Runners to recover valuables and offset losses tied to the Marathon mission.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Traxus was one of five factions available to play during the Server Slam preview event.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}}

## What Traxus offers Runners

Progressing Traxus reputation yields faction rewards such as weapon-related upgrades, Traxus-branded salvage items, and weapons.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The Traxus armory stocks a range of weapons and modification wares for purchase.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Runners earn Traxus reputation by finishing Traxus contracts and extracting while carrying valuables tied to the faction.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Several of Traxus's priority contracts are enumerated in the faction's priority contract sequence.{{cite:marathonwiki-com-priority-contracts}}

## Traxus and Night Marsh

Traxus holds Night Marsh–exclusive objectives focused on probing UESC secrets found in Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} The availability of Night Marsh and its contracts alternates with Dire Marsh throughout Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Recent changes to Traxus offerings

Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026) lowered the Armory stock for Traxus Deluxe sponsored kits and reduced the rarity of a Traxus-themed weapon from Superior to Deluxe.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} Update 1.1.9.7 (November 10, 2026) applied the same Armory reductions again, decreasing Traxus weapon availability and rarities.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} Patch 1.1.0.1 (June 9, 2026) corrected an Armory tooltip that showed the wrong cost for a Traxus Prestige modification.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}} Mid-Season 2 changes included accelerated faction progression and adjustments to sponsored kits in the Armory.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}}

