## Overview

MIDA is a Marathon faction that first appeared during the Server Slam preview period.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} GamesRadar portrays MIDA as a Mars-origin group that moved from a political organization into violent, anarchic activity.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The faction conducts its operations via an intermediary known as Gantry.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## What MIDA offers

MIDA issues contracts that Runners can complete to earn reputation and rewards.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Rank-up rewards for MIDA include equipment, MIDA Salvage items, and leg-focused implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The MIDA Armory lists grenades, gadgets, Cardio Kick, Anti-Virus Kit consumables, and Implants among its wares.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Bungie relocated faction shell upgrades into the Cradle and added faction-specific implant families; MIDA’s implant tree emphasizes mobility and disruption.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Night Marsh involvement

MIDA received Night Marsh–specific contracts with the start of Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bungie noted MIDA’s interest in uncovering what the UESC is concealing within Night Marsh’s darker areas.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Recent changes and tuning

Update 1.0.0.4 (March 11, 2026) raised the starting ammo counts in free Sponsored Kits for MIDA.{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Update 1.1.0.1 (June 9, 2026) resolved an Expose/Extinguish bug where Gantry’s voice could fail to play.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}} Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026) lowered the weekly stock of MIDA Armory Deluxe sponsored kits from three to two and removed Superior kits from the offering.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} Update 1.1.9.7 (November 10, 2026) reiterated those Armory stock reductions and further decreased themed weapon availability and rarities.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}}

