## Overview

Vandal is classified under the Combat anarchist archetype.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} The shell is designed for very fast ground movement and includes a knockback arm cannon intended to unsettle opponents during engagements.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Bungie also published a cinematic focused on the Vandal shell as part of Season 2 promotional content.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}}

## Abilities and Playstyles

Players can alter how Vandal performs by fitting different cores, implants, weapons, and mods before a run.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} For mobility-focused builds, specific cores can change the shell’s jump behavior, such as converting a double jump into a triple jump.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Implants are able to boost attributes like base movement speed, jump height, and the shell’s heat capacity.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} An alternate disruptive setup uses the Vandal’s arm cannon as a propulsion tool: firing it downward can launch the shell upward, allowing aerial repositioning and a landing that deals area damage without incurring fall damage.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Runner shells, Vandal included, support modular kits that let players vary how each archetype is approached in play.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}

## Notable Changes and Rewards

One Season 2 Bungie Rewards challenge requires players to successfully exfiltrate using Vandal to unlock the Renaissance Runner Codex Challenge.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}}

