## Archetype

Thief is presented as a Runner shell built around covert acquisitions.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} It is the sixth Runner shell and listed among the six shells planned for launch.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}}{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}}

## Abilities and Design

Thief shells are equipped with upgraded visors and a piloted butterfly-style drone intended to help locate and retrieve gear.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} They also include a Grapple Device designed to aid rapid repositioning or retreat.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} One Thief-specific core provides a second Grapple Device charge, while another core causes the Pickpocket Drone to periodically ping nearby foes when left unpiloted.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## Notable changes and rollout

Thief was not playable during the Server Slam preview but was scheduled to be available at launch.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Bungie lists a Thief Shell cinematic among other shell cinematics in Season 2 materials.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}} An update released June 9, 2026 fixed duplicated Thief voice-over lines in the Russian localization (Update 1.1.0.1).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}}

