## Archetype

Rook's archetype is Scavenger.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Rook is designed for a scavenger playstyle that lets players drop into matches already in progress.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Rook enables solo players to join in-progress matches without bringing a loadout.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## Abilities and role

Rook functions as a limited-loadout option focused on scavenging rather than risking prior progression.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} Rook is presented as a solo-focused option for players who prefer to scavenge scraps left by others.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} During Sponsored Survival, solo Rook players backfill onto maps after a period of time.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}} In Sponsored Survival, Rooks enter matches without gear, making them a low-stakes way to try the map.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}}

## Notable changes and history

Rook was included among the scavenger experience playable during the Server Slam playtest.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} A cinematic for Rook was released as part of Bungie's shell cinematics lineup.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}} An update fixed deleted backpacks when exfiling with Rook and map-display issues for Rook's position (Update 1.0.0.4, March 11, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Rook began receiving the same faction reputation bonuses solo players receive, increasing CyAc gain from exfilling (Update 1.0.0.4, March 11, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026) removed flares from Rook's kit while retaining other Nightfall inventory buffs.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

