## Setting

Perimeter is a map located at the fringe of the colony and was available in the Server Slam preview event.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} GamesRadar describes Perimeter as the most accessible map in Marathon, designed for newer players and sited on the colony’s outer areas.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}} It is one of Marathon’s three surface zones, alongside Dire Marsh and Outpost.{{cite:bungie-vidoc}} At launch the map supported matches with five-crew configurations.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}

## Layout highlights

The Symbiosis update expands Perimeter with two major new interiors: a set of subterranean tunnels called the Burrows and a flooded area known as the Reservoir.{{cite:bungie-press-symbiosis}} Symbiosis-era Perimeter is dominated by an invasive fungal biome that creates fresh traversal options across the map.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} The zone also contains a high-difficulty activity area where players can encounter a boss called the Tick Queen.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Access and rules

Perimeter was playable during Marathon’s open Server Slam preview weekend prior to release.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} During the Nightfall Refresh the developers scheduled Sponsored Perimeter rotations as part of weekend activity calendars.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Perimeter is selectable within the new Expedition PvE mode and scales in difficulty to match Expedition’s Run Series rules.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Notable changes

The Nightfall Refresh roadmap announced an upcoming expansion of Perimeter tied to the Symbiosis update.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Bungie confirmed Symbiosis would release on December 8, 2026 and include the revamped Perimeter.{{cite:bungie-press-symbiosis}} Update 1.1.9.7 listed a Sponsored Survival rotation for Perimeter running through November 17, 2026.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} Patch 1.0.0.4 (published March 11, 2026) increased how many medical cabinets and ammo crates can spawn on that map.{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}}

