## Overview

Dire Marsh is described as the colony’s agricultural research hub centered on a central complex and the Anomaly.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Dire Marsh is one of Marathon’s surface zones available at launch alongside Perimeter and Outpost.{{cite:bungie-vidoc}}

## Layout and gameplay highlights

The zone focuses on straightforward action with a central complex and serves as an epicentre for the colony’s disaster.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}} Dire Marsh has a Night variant called Night Marsh that plays slower and leans into survival horror mechanics.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Night Marsh reduces long sight lines and introduces darkness-based hazards that warp familiar landmarks and paths.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Access rules and rotation

Dire Marsh was playable in the Server Slam playtest prior to launch.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} Both Dire Marsh (Day) and Night Marsh are available at all times for the first week of Season 2, then rotate every 90 minutes thereafter.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Players who unlocked and completed Dire Marsh last season have immediate access to both variants at Season 2 start; otherwise both unlock at Runner Level 3.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Ranked weekends rotate planetside zones and can feature Dire Marsh as the zone for that weekend.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Notable changes and seasonal updates

Season 2 introduced Night Marsh alongside the Sentinel shell and the Cradle progression system.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}} Patch 1.1.0.1 (June 9, 2026) fixed Night Marsh landmark mini-map issues and certain Cert container exploits in Maintenance.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}} Expedition mode allows choosing Dire Marsh or Night Marsh for runs with similar scaling to Extraction.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Dev guidance recommended spending initial reset time exploring Perimeter and Dire Marsh in a new season.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

## See also

- [[locations|Zones of Tau Ceti IV]]

## Setting

Night Marsh is the pitch-black variant of Dire Marsh that launched with Season 2.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}} The area is designed for a slower, survival-horror pace and places extra emphasis on environmental navigation and reduced visibility.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Anomalous energy emanating from Complex affects stairways and sealed doors that lead to upper Complex areas.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Layout and mechanics highlights

Upper Complex on Night Marsh contains locked chambers behind UESC-encrypted doors that hold rarer rewards and mysteries.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Network Towers across the zone can be accessed by hacking with UESC encryption certificates called Certs to reach stockpiles and exfil points.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Complex Control features staircases to upper rooms that require Certs to open for investigation and loot.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} The Anomaly can disrupt sight lines and change how players traverse the darkness.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Darkness tools and combat changes

All Runners receive flashlights to use while on Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Darksight Scopes include a night-vision toggle that reveals nearby terrain after aiming down sights.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Vector Grenades emit lingering pulses that illuminate areas and expose nearby enemies, making them particularly useful on Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Signal Flares are available in three colors, creating persistent light sources and offering non-verbal signaling options.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

## Access rules and availability

Both Night Marsh and Dire Marsh are kept accessible throughout the first week of Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Following that initial period, the two Marsh variants alternate being available on a schedule that changes every 90 minutes.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Players who did not previously finish Dire Marsh gain access to Night Marsh once they reach Runner Level 3.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Sponsored Night Marsh events appear on a recurring timetable during special events and updates.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

## Notable changes and mode integration

Expedition Phase 1 includes Night Marsh as one of the playable zones for its roguelite PvE run series.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} The Expedition Critical Incident can require completing Upper Complex activities on Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Season 2 released Night Marsh together with the new Sentinel Runner shell and a suite of sandbox updates.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

