## Priority contracts

Priority Contracts are single-occurrence missions tied to a faction's narrative that yield higher-tier rewards such as faction weapons, backpacks, and Salvage.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}{{cite:marathonwiki-com-priority-contracts}} They function as the main vehicle for delivering story content and unlock related lore, dialogue, and cutscenes when completed.{{cite:marathonwiki-com-priority-contracts}} Priority Contracts can be completed during Expedition runs, allowing players to pursue them while playing the dedicated PvE Run Series.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Standard and Liaison contracts

Standard contracts are repeatable, single-objective tasks that provide basic faction rewards and reputation on completion.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Only one contract may be active per player at a time, and progress toward a shared contract is applied to all crew members who participate.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Liaison contracts are the one-off unlock tasks required to make a faction available for reputation gain and to allow access to that faction’s other contracts.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Season 2 adjusted Standard and Liaison contracts to ease burdensome requirements and improve rough edges, and it kept previously unlocked factions for players who finished Liaison contracts in Season 1.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 also increased the reputation awarded by Standard Contracts and lowered some upgrade material costs.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Cryo Archive contracts

When Cryo Archive is open, CyberAcme presents a weekly pool of seven distinct Cryo contracts from which players may choose.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Crews can re-roll the active Cryo contract so team members work on a common objective during a run.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Completing a Cryo contract removes it from the player’s weekly selection until the Archive returns and the pool resets.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Each completed Cryo contract grants a random, high-rarity reward such as Vault keys, materials, or gear.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Cryo Archive encounters combine puzzle elements, contested high-tier containers, and special weapon lockers for tense, competitive runs.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Season 2 reworked these contracts to permit progress to carry across multiple runs and to teach Cryo-specific mechanics, while keeping the seventh contract’s Compiler defeat requirement intact.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Season 2 contract system changes

Season 2 moved Runner shell upgrades into the Cradle, which freed faction upgrade trees and expanded Armory inventories.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Priority Contracts were shifted to emphasize direct loot rewards and no longer require specific faction reputation thresholds to access.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} The Cradle also enables players to change stat focus at any time without needing to advance a faction level.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bungie stated the season’s design intent was to make completing contracts feel more natural and less strictly linear.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Notes

Server Slam and early previews verified that multiple factions’ contracts were available to play during prelaunch testing.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}}

