## Overview

In Ranked, a crew is scored on how well it loots, fights other players, and takes calculated risks, with Holotags setting the stakes.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} It launched in a beta state during Season 1 and first ran from March 21–24, 2026.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Players progress through six rank levels, each divided into three subtiers.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Holotags and entry rules

A Holotag determines a run’s required score and the penalty applied if the crew fails to exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Holotags remain in a player’s inventory after a successful exfil and can be sold for their full credit value once exfiltration is complete.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} In the Armory, players may buy Holotags up to the tier corresponding to their current rank.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} For Season 2, queueing requires bringing a Holotag whose tier is appropriate to the player’s current rank, and the previous separate Low- and High-Stakes queues were merged into one pool that enforces a 5,000 loadout-value minimum.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Scoring and loot

A team’s combined Holotag credit value sets the run’s score target.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} The value of starting loadouts is excluded from the score target calculation.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Teams must exfil with loot equal to or exceeding that target to be awarded Ranked Points; exfiltrating below the target yields no change in RP.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Acquiring enemy Holotags or in-run Tag Chips increases overperformance capacity, allowing a crew to earn bonus RP beyond the initial target.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Loss penalties apply only when a crew fails to exfiltrate, and the penalty amount equals the team’s combined Holotag value.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Specific Holotag tiers map to set score targets and loss penalties: Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum, Diamond, and Pinnacle each have defined target and penalty values.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Tag Chips found during a run count as loot, add to overperformance capacity, and are automatically sold on exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Season 2 changes

Ranked returned in Season 2 on June 14 with a refreshed set of rewards.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} The season shortened progression times and altered how win and loss point changes scale with the average rank in a match.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 also introduced a daily Ranked Sponsored Kit that supplies a loadout appropriate to a player’s rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

