## Overview

Ranked is a competitive extraction mode in which a crew’s score depends on how well it loots, handles fights with other players, and takes calculated risks.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Entry and Holotags

Entering a Ranked run requires bringing a Holotag, an item that defines both the score target and the penalty for failing the run.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Holotags remain in a player’s inventory after a successful exfil and may be sold for their full credit value following exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} The Armory sells Holotags up to the tier corresponding to a player’s current rank.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} For Season 2, players must queue with a Holotag whose tier corresponds to their active rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Scoring and Ranked Points

A crew’s combined Holotag values determine the run’s score target that the team must reach to gain Ranked Points.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} The value of items in a player’s starting loadout is not included in that score target calculation.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Exfiltrating with loot equal to or above the score target awards Ranked Points, while returning with less than the target produces no change in RP.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} The amount a team risks losing on a failed run is set by the combined Holotag value of the crew, and RP is deducted only when the team does not successfully exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Tag Chips and enemy Holotags function as loot that contributes toward the score target, provide a means to increase the crew’s capacity to earn bonus points beyond the initial target, and are automatically sold on exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Ranks and Season 2 changes

The Ranked ladder consists of six rank names—Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum, Diamond, and Pinnacle—each subdivided into three tiers.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Ranked first ran as a beta weekend from March 21–24, 2026 during Season 1.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Season 2 relaunched Ranked on June 14 with updates to rewards and progression.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} In Season 2 the previously separate Low and High Stakes queues were merged into a single queue and a minimum Loadout value of 5,000 was introduced.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Progression was tuned to be quicker and the system for awarding or subtracting points was adjusted to account for average match rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 also added a daily Ranked Sponsored Kit that supplies a loadout appropriate to a player’s rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

