## Overview

Bungie introduced the Cradle as a Season 2 feature that lets players direct how their Runner shells develop over the course of the season.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}}{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}}

Season 2 announcement material describes the Cradle as the interface for improving Runner shell statistics during the season.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}}

## How the Cradle Works

Season 2 documentation states the Cradle leverages WEAVEworms to construct biocybernetic shell bodies and to boost Runner shell attributes across six distinct categories.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

Players feed the Matter Converter with weapons, equipment, and other gear to generate experience that advances the Cradle.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

As the Cradle gains levels, it awards Energy that can be assigned to any of the six stat categories.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

Assigned Energy may be moved between stats at any time without incurring penalties or restrictions.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

Cradle advancement is accessible by all Runner shells as a single shared progression track and is cleared when a new season begins.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}}

## Related Systems and Design

Season 2 reworked implants so that each implant is defined by one fixed perk and a matching, fixed stat configuration.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

Bungie relocated Runner shell upgrades from individual faction progression trees into the Cradle to consolidate where shell improvements are obtained.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

With those shell upgrades centralized, faction progression trees were expanded to provide a broader set of Armory options and distinct implant families.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Future and Reworks

In October, Bungie performed a progression reset that returned Cradle enhancements and faction aftermarket upgrades to their default states as part of a live-service refresh.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

Bungie’s roadmap indicates a refactored Cradle and more extensive shell progression are planned for the larger March update that will connect multiple systems.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

The December Symbiosis update is scheduled to add a permanent PvE experience, expand the Perimeter, introduce a new Runner shell, and improve onboarding ahead of the March integration.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

