## Overview

The Armory sells Holotags for use in Ranked queues; these Holotags are bought with Credits.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}  Season 2 relocated many Runner shell upgrade paths into the Cradle, which freed space for the Armory to broaden its available options.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## What the Armory Sells and Barters

CyberAcme's Armory inventory focuses on starter and basic supplies such as weapons, backpacks, ammunition, healing items, and keys.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}  NuCaloric's Armory stock emphasizes restorative items and survivability gear, including consumables that heal, self-revive items, shields, and implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}  Traxus's Armory places greater weight on weapons and a larger selection of modification items.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}  In Season 2, certain Schema items began to unlock new barter options within the Armory.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Sponsored Kits and Ranked

Season 2 added a daily Sponsored Kit for Ranked that provides a loadout appropriate to a player's rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}  Update 1.1.9.2 made Weapon and Backpack Schema items in the Armory require Credits.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}  Update 1.1.9.7 reduced weekly Deluxe sponsored kit stock for MIDA and Traxus and removed their Superior sponsored kits.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}}  At the Season 2 launch, players received CyberAcme Sponsored Kits tied to their Season 1 Runner Level, ranging from an Enhanced kit at level 10 up to Deluxe at level 50 and Superior at level 75.{{cite:kotaku-season-2}}  To enter Ranked queues a Holotag must be carried in the backpack; the Armory sells Holotags for Credits.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Cryo Archive Sponsored Kit

Players who meet the entry requirements for Cryo Archive can collect a single Cryo Archive Sponsored Kit at the Armory, usable once.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}  That kit is a blue-tier bundle configured to support an early attempt at Cryo Archive content.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

