## Overview

Cores are upgrades tied to individual Runner shells that alter or enhance those shells' abilities.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Players build each shell's role by equipping cores together with implants, weapons, and mods.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## How cores change abilities

One Thief core provides an extra charge for the Grapple Device.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} A different Thief core causes the Pickpocket Drone to emit periodic pings at nearby foes when it is not being piloted.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} For Vandal, a core option can replace the double jump with a triple jump to prioritize movement.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Another Vandal configuration can convert the arm cannon into a downward-fired self-propel that launches the shell and creates area damage at the landing site.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## Seasonal and faction context

At launch, cores are part of the loot pool alongside weapons, mods, and implants.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Season updates add new content sets that may include cores in addition to weapons, mods, implants, and Runner shells.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Season 2 introduces a complete set of ten Sentinel-specific Runner cores available across rarity tiers.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Sekiguchi Genetics' Armory inventory includes Marathon Cores among its offerings.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## Acquisition and rewards

During the Server Slam open preview, the Standard Arrival Cache awarded Standard Runner shell cores to players who completed the introductory mission.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Enhanced and Deluxe Arrival Caches granted Enhanced and Deluxe Runner shell cores respectively as players reached higher progression thresholds during the event.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} GamesRadar likens high-impact weapon chip mods to Marathon Cores in how they can dramatically change a tool's function.{{cite:gamesradar-weapons}}

