## Overview

In Season 1, implants granted stat packages and also carried a random perk.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Server Slam arrival caches included multiple implants across rarity tiers for players to unlock at launch.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}}

## Season 2 rework

Season 2 changes refocused implants to prioritize a single perk with fixed stats as a secondary element.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Every implant now grants one fixed perk and carries a fixed stat package reflected in the implant name.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Some implants will only appear at higher rarities to balance high-utility perks.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Implant stat benefits continue to scale with rarity from gray through gold.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 added eight new implant perks, including Going Dark which grants invisibility during healing consumable use.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

## Faction implant families

Each faction tree now contains a unique family of head, torso, and leg implants aligned to that faction's playstyle.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## See also

- [[cores|Cores]]

## Overview

Implant power scales with rarity tiers that run from gray up to gold.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Some implants will only exist at higher rarity tiers after the Season 2 change.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Named rarities and colours

Bungie names a Standard tier in Server Slam reward caches.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Bungie names an Enhanced tier and labels it Green in Server Slam rewards.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Bungie names a Deluxe tier and labels it Blue in Server Slam rewards.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}}

## Additional notes

Season 2 made implants defined by their perk first and gave them fixed stats.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 reduced some items' rarity from Superior to Deluxe in Armory updates (Update 1.1.9.2, October 6, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

