## Overview

The UESC are security forces operating on Tau Ceti IV who oppose Runners.{{cite:marathon-official-site}} Bungie states the UESC have increased security measures on Tau Ceti IV in Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} The derelict UESC Marathon ship includes intense UESC security encounters in Cryo Archive.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Role and Behavior

UESC patrol Tau Ceti IV with humanoid combat robots and drones that attack intruders.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} UESC units drop items that can grant encryption certificates used to access Night Marsh resources and exfils.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 increased credits rewarded for killing UESC when using the Bounty Hunter chip.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

## Encounters and Tuning

Cryo Archive presents high-intensity encounters against UESC with labyrinthine cryopods and security puzzles.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Developers reduced most UESC enemy health by about 10–15% and UESC boss shield HP by 25% in Update 1.0.0.4 (March 11, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026) reduced UESC aggression and UESC damage to runners in Solo playlists.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

## Community Interaction

Runners and companies formed a non-aggression pact to counter increased UESC security measures.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} The Outpost map is set in a UESC military installation with dedicated UESC security presence.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}}

